(]. People )Tj
-37.41 -1.343 Td
(who know the patterns gain insight into the framework faster. Even peopl\e who don't know the patterns can )Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(benefit from the structure they lend to the framework's documentation. E\nhancing documentation is )Tj
T*
(important for all types of software, but it's particularly important for\ frameworks. Frameworks often pose a )Tj
T*
(steep learning curve that must be overcome before they're useful. While \design patterns might not flatten )Tj
T*
(the learning curve entirely, they can make it less steep by making key e\lements of the framework's design )Tj
T*
(more explicit.)Tj
0 -2.557 TD
(Because patterns and frameworks have some similarities, people often won\der how or even if they differ. )Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(They are different in three major ways:)Tj
1.607 -2.557 Td
(1.  )Tj
/T1_1 1 Tf
(Design patterns are more abstract than frameworks.)Tj
/T1_0 1 Tf
( Frameworks can be embodied in code, but only )Tj
/T1_1 1 Tf
1.25 -1.2 Td
(examples)Tj
/T1_0 1 Tf
( of patterns can be embodied in code. A strength of frameworks is that t\hey can be written )Tj
T*
(down in programming languages and not only studied but executed and reus\ed directly. In contrast, )Tj
T*
(the design patterns in this book have to be implemented each time they'r\e used. Design patterns also )Tj
T*
(explain the intent, trade-offs, and consequences of a design.)Tj
-1.25 -2.557 Td
(2.  )Tj
/T1_1 1 Tf
(Design patterns are smaller architectural elements than frameworks.)Tj
/T1_0 1 Tf
( A typical framework contains )Tj
1.25 -1.2 Td
(several design patterns, but the reverse is never true.)Tj
-1.25 -2.557 Td
(3.  )Tj
/T1_1 1 Tf
(Design patterns are less specialized than frameworks.)Tj
/T1_0 1 Tf
( Frameworks always have a particular )Tj
1.25 -1.2 Td
(application domain. A graphical editor framework might be used in a fact\ory simulation, but it won't )Tj
T*
(be mistaken for a simulation framework. In contrast, the design patterns\ in this catalog can be used )Tj
T*
(in nearly any kind of application. While more specialized design pattern\s than ours are certainly )Tj
T*
(possible \(say, design patterns for distributed systems or concurrent pr\ogramming\), even these )Tj
T*
(wouldn't dictate an application architecture like a framework would.)Tj
-2.857 -2.557 Td
(Frameworks are becoming increasingly common and important. They are the \way that object-oriented )Tj
0 -1.2 TD
(systems achieve the most reuse. Larger object-oriented applications will\ end up consisting of layers of )Tj
T*
(frameworks that cooperate with each other. Most of the design and code i\n the application will come from )Tj
T*
(or be influenced by the frameworks it uses.)Tj
